Without a Third Variable – Using Arithmetic OperationsThe idea is to store sum in a variable so that we can get both values without third variable.Let us understand with an example, a = 10, b = 20Store the sum of a and b in a, a = a + b = 10 + 20 = 30Get the original value of a and store it in b, b = a - b = 30 - 20 = 10Get the original value of b and store it in a, a = a - b = 30 - 10 = 20Final result: a = 20, b = 10
