Without a Third Variable – Using Bitwise XORThe idea is to use the properties of XOR to swap the two variables. Let us understand with an example, a = 10, b = 20Store the XOR of a and b in a, a = a ^ b = 10 ^ 20 = 30Get the original value of a and store it in b, b = a ^ b = 30 ^ 20 = 10Get the original value of b and store it in a, a = a ^ b = 30 ^ 10 = 20Final result: a = 20, b = 10
            C++

    // C++ Code to swap two numbers using bitwise XOR
#include <iostream>
using namespace std;

